---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { totalCheats } from '../data/games';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
const total = totalCheats();
const schema = [
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'AboutPage', name: `About ${SITE.name}`, url: new URL('/about/', Astro.site).href },
];
---

<Base
  title="About GTA Cheat Codes & How We Check Codes"
  description="Who runs GTA Cheat Codes, how every cheat is sourced and checked, how PlayStation combos are converted to Xbox and Switch, and how to report a wrong code."
  schema={schema}
>
  <article class="wrap page">
    <p class="kicker">About & methodology</p>
    <h1 class="display">Built by players, <span class="grad-text">for players</span></h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        {SITE.name} is an independent fan resource for Grand Theft Auto cheat codes. We cover GTA 5, San Andreas, Vice City,
        GTA 4, GTA 3, the Definitive Edition trilogy and the handheld spin-offs, and we keep a page tracking GTA 6. The
        structured database currently holds {total} codes.
      </p>
      <h2>How codes are sourced and checked</h2>
      <p>
        Every cheat for GTA 5, San Andreas, Vice City, GTA 4 and GTA 3 lives in one structured database. Each entry stores
        the PlayStation button sequence, the PC code and any phone number. The tables, the Cheat Finder, the Combo Trainer
        and the Cheat Roulette all read from it, so a code can't say one thing on one page and something else on another.
      </p>
      <p>
        Codes are cross-checked against long-standing community references. Where a code differs between releases, or a
        console version couldn't be confirmed, the entry says so or leaves the console code out instead of guessing. Codes
        for Liberty City Stories, Vice City Stories and Chinatown Wars were checked against at least two independent
        references.
      </p>
      <h2>How Xbox and Switch combos are generated</h2>
      <p>The games map cheats button for button across controllers. We store the PlayStation sequence and convert it:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Xbox:</strong> Cross → A, Circle → B, Square → X, Triangle → Y, L1 → LB, R1 → RB, L2 → LT, R2 → RT.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Switch (Definitive Edition):</strong> Cross → B, Circle → A, Square → Y, Triangle → X, L1 → L, R1 → R, L2 → ZL,
          R2 → ZR.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What we will never do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Publish "GTA Online cheats", money generators or mod menus. Single-player cheats don't work online, and tools
          that claim otherwise are scams or get accounts banned.
        </li>
        <li>Invent codes for unreleased games. The GTA 6 page only reports what has been confirmed.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Found a wrong code?</h2>
      <p>
        If a code doesn't work on your copy, note the game, the platform and the version (original, remaster or Definitive
        Edition). Release differences are the most common cause, and we'll update the entry.
      </p>
      <h2>Not affiliated</h2>
      <p>
        Grand Theft Auto, Rockstar Games and all related names and marks belong to Take-Two Interactive Software. This site
        is not affiliated with or endorsed by them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-top: 48px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(44px, 6.5vw, 80px);
    margin: 12px 0 10px;
    max-width: 16ch;
  }
</style>
